WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.597
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for writing a first sentence.

2
00:00:04.047 --> 00:00:11.424
The goal is a child who writes a sentence never written before, with a capital, spaces and a period, and reads it back.

3
00:00:12.024 --> 00:00:17.712
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

4
00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:22.876
This plan is for a child who can write some short words, but not a sentence.

5
00:00:23.326 --> 00:00:26.098
Often the words run together, with no spaces.

6
00:00:26.548 --> 00:00:30.426
Or there is no capital and no period, or no idea of their own.

7
00:00:30.876 --> 00:00:38.551
A sentence asks for many things at once: an idea, every word, and three marks. While one gets attention, the others slip.

8
00:00:39.351 --> 00:00:41.264
So this plan takes them one at a time.

9
00:00:41.714 --> 00:00:43.183
First, say it and count it.

10
00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:46.455
Then the capital and the period, and then the spaces.

11
00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:50.541
Then sentence frames, and then sentences of your child's own.

12
00:00:50.991 --> 00:00:52.984
And day ten is the final check.

13
00:00:53.784 --> 00:01:01.013
Every sentence follows the same four steps. Say it. Count it. One line for each word. Write it and read it back.

14
00:01:01.463 --> 00:01:07.375
Every word in the book can be sounded out, apart from seven words you tell. They are listed in the guide.

15
00:01:08.075 --> 00:01:13.361
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about five minutes.
